{"nodes": [{"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_final_recap_experience", "label": "Final Recap Experience", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Played after all 3 curriculum terms, mostly self-directed over the holidays. Must touch everything taught across the year in one 20-30 min sitting, so it is ordered for narrative pacing rather than Term 1-2-3 calendar order.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a70", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_one_game_one_entry_point", "label": "One Game, One App, One Entry Point", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Corrected from an earlier two-separate-apps decision. Content is fully separate per band (different scenarios, different mechanics for 2 of 5 realms) but delivered as a single product; the separation lives in content data and component logic, not app architecture.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a70", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_band_split", "label": "P1-P3 / P4-P6 Band Split", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The Atlas Gate asks the student which band they are in; every downstream screen reads content from the schema using that value (band: 'lower' | 'higher').", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_term_1_healthy_digital_habits", "label": "Term 1 - Healthy Digital Habits", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Four core habits: Set Boundaries Online, Think Before You Act, Report Inappropriate Content, Engage and Support. Written as one unified curriculum for all of P1-P6, with no band split.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_term_2_recess_activities", "label": "Term 2 - Recess Activities", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Reinforcement plus pledge: Be Safe / Be Kind / Be Smart Online, Balance is Key, When Things Go Wrong. Also unified across P1-P6.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_term_3_fake_news_and_images", "label": "Term 3 - Fake News and Images", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The only place the Overview Plan itself splits by band. Hook: 'Can our eyes be fooled?' covering fake news and fake/altered images.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_stop_and_check", "label": "STOP & CHECK Method (P1-P3)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "STOP - pause; CHECK - ask a trusted adult or check another source. The lower band's media-literacy framework for Fable Falls.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_sure_framework", "label": "S.U.R.E. Framework (P4-P6)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Source / Understand / Research / Evaluate. The higher band's media-literacy framework for Fable Falls.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_cyber_defender_quest", "label": "Cyber Defender Quest", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Confirmed 18 Aug 2026 as the capstone activity name (not 'Cyber Detective Quest' as earlier drafts suggested); built as the P4-P6 Fable Falls mini-game's title.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_fable_falls", "label": "Fable Falls Realm", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The fifth realm, covering fake news and altered images. Name resolved 18 Aug 2026 and shipped the same day by working around the unsourced official content rather than waiting on it. Carries a 5th accent colour (--sage) and stamp icon (eye).", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_the_echo", "label": "The Echo", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Fable Falls' guide character - repeats whatever it hears without checking it, the personification of a rumour rather than a villain, consistent with the cast's no-villain rule.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_digital_footprint_gap", "label": "Digital Footprint / Positive Digital Trail", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Top-priority content gap: appears in both Term 1 (Think Before You Act) and Term 2 (Be Smart Online), so two independent source mentions. Fixed as a decision beat inside Bully Bog alongside the kindness choice, since the curriculum pairs 'respectful' and 'positive trail' in one sentence.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_report_and_block", "label": "Report & Block Resolution Option", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Given a reusable resolution option at the redirect moment in every realm rather than a dedicated realm, because the curriculum itself always pairs it with another habit and never treats it standalone.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_engage_and_support", "label": "Engage and Support", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A named Term 1 habit with no clear home; addressed by giving Comet an explicit 'who would you tell?' prompt at Bully Bog's bystander moment, reinforcing that seeking help is itself a habit, not just a fallback.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_plagiarism_ip_gap", "label": "Respect Others' Work (Plagiarism / IP)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Smallest gap - one bullet under Be Smart Online. Planned to fold into Fable Falls' Understand/Research step as a light touch, but the shipped content does not yet touch it; still the lowest-priority gap.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_three_tips_to_check", "label": "3 Tips to CHECK (Unsourced SLS Content)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A missing source-material gap rather than a design gap - it lives in the SLS lesson package, not the Overview Plan. Worked around with general media-literacy signals (source credibility, cross-checking, does-it-add-up reasoning), flagged in realms.js as a placeholder pending swap-in. Low risk either way since it is just data.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_realm_plan_by_band", "label": "Realm Plan by Band", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Maps each of the five realms to a P1-P3 and a P4-P6 mechanic and framing, plus Report & Block as a universal addition wherever a redirect moment happens.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_suggested_play_order", "label": "Suggested Play Order per Band", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Open with each band's own signature classroom scenario so the recap lands as 'remember this?', middle realms in either order, Fake News last as a synthesis challenge drawing on judgement built earlier, then the Pledge. Free exploration stays; this is a default, not a gate.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_band_differentiation_is_enrichment", "label": "Band Differentiation as Design Enrichment", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Harder mechanics, more nuanced scenarios and different stakes for P4-P6 are the team's own design extension, not curriculum-mandated - Terms 1 and 2 are one-size-fits-all and only Term 3 splits by band. The Luke vs Sam & Tom split began as a suggestion in the Lesson Plan doc and hardened only in later slide decks. Disclosed as a design choice and confirmed age-appropriate by the school contact.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a71a", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_p4_5_vs_p4_6_resolution", "label": "P4-5 vs P4-6 Resolution", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The source doc writes the S.U.R.E. band as '(P4-5)' consistently in all three places it appears. Decision 18 Aug 2026: treat P4-5 as P4-6, so all of P4-P6 gets S.U.R.E. with no special-casing P6 out.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a71a", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_fifth_pledge_line", "label": "Fifth Traveler's Pledge Line", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "'I'll stop and check before I believe or share.' - the Fable Falls line, live in the certificate as of 18 Aug 2026 now that activePledge() no longer filters it out. Wording sign-off remains informally open.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_final_recap_experience", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_suggested_play_order", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_one_game_one_entry_point", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_band_split", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a70", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_band_split", "target": "storyline_atlas_gate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Improvement_Plan.md", "source_location": "\u00a70", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvemen